CORE dfcc-only
main.c
--dfcc main --apply-loop-contracts
^\[foo\.loop_assigns\.\d+\] line 17 Check assigns clause inclusion for loop .*: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.\d+\] line 32 cond: SUCCESS$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
--
The condition of a conditional target in a loop assigns clause calls valid,
which calls cond. Only cond is reachable from main and hence instrumented. The
code that DFCC generates for the loop assigns clause inlines the original bodies
of both functions. It used to inline the instrumented body of cond into the body
of valid, where the call to cond does not pass a write set, and failed with "not
enough arguments when inlining goto program".
